Let $u<i$ be integers and let $\xi\in H^0(\mathcal O(iD)/\mathcal O(uD))$ be nonzero. There is an integer $t$ with $u<t\leq i$ such that local lifts of $\xi$ have pole order exactly $tm_\alpha$ at every $D_\alpha$. Those lifts give a trivializing section of $\mathcal O(tD)$ on $(t-u)D$. In particular, $$\label{eq:scalar-endpoint}
 g_s^0(i;\mathcal O_V)=
 \begin{cases}
 1,&\mathcal O(iD)|_{sD}\simeq\mathcal O_{sD},\\
 0,&\text{otherwise}.
 \end{cases}$$

The scalar widths satisfy $$\label{eq:limiting-width}
 a_*=\lim_{e\to\infty}\frac{d_e}{M_e}
 =\frac{p}{p+1},\qquad Dc_2(V)=0.$$
